message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Libya Automated Land-Cover Mapping"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sabzchi Dehkharghani"
    given-names: "Hamed"
version: 1.0.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22770165"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hamedsabzchi/libya-automated-land-cover-mapping"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22770165"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible Google Earth Engine and Python workflow for guided automated
  land-cover mapping in Libya using annual Google Satellite Embedding features,
  SRTM terrain predictors, Random Forest classification, stratified hold-out
  validation, and explicit multi-year temporal decision rules.
keywords:
  - Google Earth Engine
  - land cover
  - remote sensing
  - geospatial
  - Random Forest
  - Satellite Embedding
  - AlphaEarth Foundations
  - Libya
